<mjml><mj-head><mj-title>GatorBait Magazine: Friday Pregame, Florida at Missouri</mj-title><mj-preview>Franz Beard leads the Friday pregame edition: the Sooth Board, three keys and who is out.</mj-preview><mj-attributes><mj-all font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" /><mj-text color="#11274A" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5" /><mj-button background-color="#FA4616" color="#FFFFFF" border-radius="3px" font-size="15px" font-weight="800" /></mj-attributes></mj-head><mj-body background-color="#EEF1F5">
<mj-section background-color="#FA4616" padding="8px 16px"><mj-column><mj-text align="center" color="#FFFFFF" font-size="13px" font-weight="800" padding="0">TEST EMAIL for Brenden only. Not sent to the list.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="0"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_12f2b9b8ad7b4a7b99b66dabc7e694ea~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_1600,al_c,q_85/file.jpg" alt="GatorBait Magazine cover: Gators head to Missouri, where history hasn’t been kind. Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-soothsayer-gators-head-to-missouri-where-history-hasn-t-been-kind" padding="0" width="600px" /></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="22px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="17px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 6px">No. 8 Florida (4-0) is 2-4 in Columbia since 2012 and has to find an emotional peak right after the biggest win in years. Franz Beard asks if the Gators are tough enough.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-soothsayer-gators-head-to-missouri-where-history-hasn-t-been-kind" padding="14px 0 6px">READ THE COLUMN</mj-button><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" background-color="#081F3D" padding="6px 0 10px">OPEN THE FULL MAGAZINE</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="0"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_1fe245369e1d40dfbe9ab7c20053de72~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_760,al_c,q_85/file.jpg" alt="No. 8 Florida (4-0) at No. 25 Missouri (3-1), Saturday, Oct. 3, 3:30 p.m. ET on ABC. Line FLA -5.5, total 57.5." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" padding="0" width="600px" /></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="12px 24px 16px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#D7E0EB" font-size="14px" line-height="1.5" padding="0">ESPN matchup predictor: Florida 70.2%, Missouri 29.8%. 71°, 0% chance of rain, gusts to 10 mph (ESPN forecast, Oct. 1)</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="24px 24px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 4px">FOR THE STAT GEEKS</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="30px" line-height="1.1" font-weight="900" padding="0 0 4px">Tale of the tape</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="13px" padding="0 0 8px">Season averages, four games each. Orange marks the edge. Source: ESPN.</mj-text><mj-table padding="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td style="padding:6px 4px;border-bottom:3px solid #0A2CA8;font-size:14px;font-weight:900;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1px;">FLORIDA</td><td style="border-bottom:3px solid #081F3D;"></td><td style="padding:6px 4px;border-bottom:3px solid #F1B82D;text-align:right;font-size:14px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;letter-spacing:1px;">MISSOURI</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">53.5</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">POINTS PER GAME</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">35.8</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">22.8</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">POINTS ALLOWED</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">20.8</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">532.8</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">TOTAL YARDS PER GAME</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">418.8</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">260.0</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">RUSHING YARDS PER GAME</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">155.8</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">5.9</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">YARDS PER CARRY</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">4.2</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">10.5</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">YARDS PER PASS ATTEMPT</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">8.6</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">73.1%</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">COMPLETION %</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">64.2%</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">47.7%</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">THIRD-DOWN CONVERSIONS</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">40.7%</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">40.6%</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">OPPONENT THIRD DOWNS</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">32.2%</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">12</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">SACKS BY THE DEFENSE</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">12</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">23</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">TACKLES FOR LOSS</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">20</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:left;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">100.0%</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;color:#4B586A;">FIELD GOAL %</td><td style="padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;text-align:right;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;width:26%;">62.5%</td></tr></mj-table></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="16px 24px 4px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 4px">PLAYERS TO KNOW</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="13px" padding="0">Season leaders by jersey number. Source: ESPN.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="6px 24px 8px"><mj-column background-color="#0A2CA8" padding="18px 18px 20px" vertical-align="top"><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="22px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1px" padding="0">FLORIDA</mj-text><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">PASSING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#12 Aaron Philo, QB</mj-text><mj-text color="#DCE4FF" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">63 of 87, 917 yards, 7 TD, 2 INT</mj-text><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">RUSHING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#13 Jadan Baugh, RB</mj-text><mj-text color="#DCE4FF" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">83 carries, 600 yards, 11 TD</mj-text><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">RECEIVING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#1 Vernell Brown III, WR</mj-text><mj-text color="#DCE4FF" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">17 catches, 271 yards, 2 TD</mj-text><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">SACKS</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#0 Jayden Woods, LB</mj-text><mj-text color="#DCE4FF" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">4</mj-text><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">TACKLES</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#5 Myles Graham, LB</mj-text><mj-text color="#DCE4FF" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">28</mj-text></mj-column><mj-column background-color="#111111" padding="18px 18px 20px" vertical-align="top"><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="22px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1px" padding="0">MISSOURI</mj-text><mj-text color="#F1B82D" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">PASSING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#13 Austin Simmons, QB</mj-text><mj-text color="#E9D9A8" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">70 of 107, 947 yards, 11 TD</mj-text><mj-text color="#F1B82D" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">RUSHING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#20 Jamal Roberts, RB</mj-text><mj-text color="#E9D9A8" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">89 carries, 395 yards, 3 TD</mj-text><mj-text color="#F1B82D" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">RECEIVING</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#19 Cayden Lee, WR</mj-text><mj-text color="#E9D9A8" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">27 catches, 412 yards, 4 TD</mj-text><mj-text color="#F1B82D" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">SACKS</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#10 Daeden Hopkins, EDGE</mj-text><mj-text color="#E9D9A8" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">6</mj-text><mj-text color="#F1B82D" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="12px 0 0">TACKLES</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="19px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="2px 0 0">#5 Nicholas Rodriguez, LB</mj-text><mj-text color="#E9D9A8" font-size="13px" line-height="1.4" padding="2px 0 0">39</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="4px 24px 24px"><mj-column><mj-button href="https://floridagators.com/sports/football/roster" background-color="#081F3D" padding="6px 0 0">THE FULL GATORS ROSTER</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="26px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 6px">THE SOOTHSAYER</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="30px" line-height="1.1" font-weight="900" padding="0 0 4px">The Sooth Board</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" padding="0 0 8px">Franz Beard picks every SEC game. Here are three. Lines: ESPN.</mj-text><mj-table padding="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;background:#FFF4EF;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">3:30 P.M. &#183; ABC</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">No. 8 Florida (4-0) at No. 25 Missouri (3-1)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line FLA -5.5 &#183; O/U 57.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Florida by more than 5.5</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">NOON &#183; ABC</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">No. 7 Alabama (4-0) at No. 16 Mississippi State (4-0)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line ALA -6 &#183; O/U 60.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Alabama</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">12:45 P.M. &#183; SEC NETWORK</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">Vanderbilt (3-1) at No. 2 Georgia (4-0)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line UGA -25.5 &#183; O/U 50.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Georgia</div></td></tr></mj-table><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" background-color="#081F3D" padding="14px 0 4px">SEE ALL 7 OF FRANZ&#8217;S PICKS</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="18px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-divider border-color="#dde3ec" border-width="1px" padding="0 0 12px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0">THREE KEYS</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">1. Baugh against a top-20 run defense</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Florida runs for 260 yards a game and has 18 rushing touchdowns, tied for most in the country.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">2. Philo’s shots against a bend-don’t-break secondary</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Aaron Philo’s 10.5 yards an attempt leads the SEC and he has been sacked twice in 104 throws.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">3. Third downs and Austin Simmons</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Florida allows 248 passing yards a game, 113th nationally, and opponents convert 41% on third down.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="14px 24px 22px"><mj-column><mj-divider border-color="#dde3ec" border-width="1px" padding="0 0 12px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0">WHO IS OUT</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="13px" padding="2px 0 0">As of Oct. 1. ESPN lists no injuries for either team; names below are GatorBait reporting.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="17px" font-weight="900" padding="10px 0 2px">Florida</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.6" padding="0 0 4px">WR Vernell Brown III &#8212; <b>Questionable</b><br/>WR Bailey Stockton &#8212; <b>Questionable</b></mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="17px" font-weight="900" padding="10px 0 2px">Missouri</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.6" padding="0 0 4px">S JaDon Blair &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>RB Ahmad Hardy &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>RB Malae Fonoti &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>OL Josh Atkins &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>TE Gavin Hoffman &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>EDGE Langden Kitchen &#8212; <b>Questionable</b><br/>EDGE Darris Smith &#8212; <b>Questionable</b></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="26px 24px 4px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 4px">THIS WEEK</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="28px" font-weight="900" padding="0">More from GatorBait</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="20px 18px 6px"><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_408fa442a2d54309aa66050fb0f4d35e~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Jon Sumrall reacts on the Florida sideline with an official in the foreground (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/coaches-and-fans-have-different-playbooks-so-have-another-round-thirsty-gators" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">BUDDY MARTIN · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/coaches-and-fans-have-different-playbooks-so-have-another-round-thirsty-gators" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">Coaches and Fans Have Different Playbooks. So Have Another Round, Thirsty Gators.</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">Florida fans have earned the right to brag after four years of misery. Just don’t build a shrine on an early poll before Saturday’s trip to Missouri.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/coaches-and-fans-have-different-playbooks-so-have-another-round-thirsty-gators" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_56a64986c874417c9a8299fae22649ed~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Buddy Martin column: The Looming Brilliance of Buster Faulkner. Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media; Faulkner photo UAA." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-looming-brilliance-of-buster-faulkner-if-it-works-one-time-we-retire-it" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">BUDDY MARTIN · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-looming-brilliance-of-buster-faulkner-if-it-works-one-time-we-retire-it" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">The Looming Brilliance of Buster Faulkner: “If It Works Once, We Retire It”</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">This guy could turn out to be brilliant. Maybe even Steve Spurrier brilliant. But Faulkner has to earn that.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-looming-brilliance-of-buster-faulkner-if-it-works-one-time-we-retire-it" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="6px 18px 6px"><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_f130d47a9cb74914b869ac554c67e931~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Officials at the SEC replay monitor on the Florida sideline (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/florida-keeps-winning-big-and-the-laundry-keeps-piling-up" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">ANALYSIS · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/florida-keeps-winning-big-and-the-laundry-keeps-piling-up" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">Florida Keeps Winning Big, and the Laundry Keeps Piling Up</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">The No. 8 Gators have outscored four opponents by nearly 31 points a game while drawing 35 flags for 357 yards.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/florida-keeps-winning-big-and-the-laundry-keeps-piling-up" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_00359caad82744778e7c387d8bf98777~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Aaron Philo, Florida quarterback (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/when-it-came-to-finding-a-quarterback-sumrall-trusted-buster-and-it-paid-off" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">FRANZ BEARD · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/when-it-came-to-finding-a-quarterback-sumrall-trusted-buster-and-it-paid-off" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">When it came to finding a quarterback Sumrall trusted Buster and it paid off</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">Aaron Philo was barely known when the season began. Jon Sumrall trusted Buster Faulkner to find a quarterback, and it paid off.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/when-it-came-to-finding-a-quarterback-sumrall-trusted-buster-and-it-paid-off" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="6px 18px 6px"><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_dc70ea9e65574abebd3b0ace40bd8232~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.png" alt="Jayden Woods, Florida JACK linebacker (Graphic: GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/jayden-woods-added-to-chuck-bednarik-award-watch-list" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">HONORS · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/jayden-woods-added-to-chuck-bednarik-award-watch-list" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">Jayden Woods Added To Chuck Bednarik Award Watch List</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">The sophomore JACK’s 19 tackles, six TFLs and four sacks through four games have him in the running for college football’s top defensive honor.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/jayden-woods-added-to-chuck-bednarik-award-watch-list" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column><mj-column padding="0 6px 12px" vertical-align="top"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_a67ff355ad6a4d668106c2befa41b208~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_640,h_360,al_c,q_80/file.png" alt="Show-Me State of Mind: No. 8 Florida at No. 25 Missouri, Saturday, Oct. 3, 3:30 p.m. ET. GatorBait Media graphic." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/first-look-missouri-florida-gators-show-me-state-of-mind" padding="0" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="11px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="10px 2px 0">PREVIEW · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="18px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="4px 2px 0"><a href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/first-look-missouri-florida-gators-show-me-state-of-mind" style="color:#081F3D;text-decoration:none;">Show-Me State of Mind: A First Look at No. 25 Missouri</a></mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.45" padding="6px 2px 0">No. 8 Florida’s reward for routing Ole Miss is a trip to No. 25 Missouri, which let a fourth-quarter lead get away at Mississippi State.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/first-look-missouri-florida-gators-show-me-state-of-mind" align="left" padding="10px 2px 0" inner-padding="9px 18px" font-size="13px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="6px 24px 26px"><mj-column><mj-text align="center" color="#11274A" font-size="16px" padding="0 0 6px">Next up: South Carolina, Oct. 10, in The Swamp. Then Texas in Austin on Oct. 17.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" padding="8px 0 0">OPEN THE FULL MAGAZINE</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#060B1C" padding="0"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_51b0e0af194647cf97759206af475e82~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_812,al_c,q_85/file.jpg" alt="Best shots from Florida 52, Ole Miss 28: a touchdown celebration, Jon Sumrall leading the Gators out, the defense swarming, The Swamp at kickoff and the scene after the win. Photos by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" width="600px" /></mj-column></mj-section><mj-section background-color="#060B1C" padding="10px 24px 18px"><mj-column><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" background-color="#060B1C" border="2px solid #FA4616" padding="0">SEE THE FULL GALLERY</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
